[size=5][b]Map Resource Markers[/b][/size]

Pick what you are looking for in the map's Filters menu, and the map shows where it is: trees, ore veins, fishing and digging spots, herbs and food, the animals whose parts upgrade your gear, the enemy factions of your "Kill N" challenges, and treasure chests.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]A Markers panel in the map's Filters menu:[/b] one button per type, above the game's own filters. Click a button (or press A on it) and its markers appear on the map; hover it for the name.[/*]
[*][b]Harvesting:[/b] Pine, Spruce and Birch; Copper, Iron and Silver Ore; digging spots; Carp, Trout and Gangrenous Eel, and Bass fishing spots.[/*]
[*][b]Cooking:[/b] fish, Artemisia, Dracaena and Lithops herbs, Mushrooms, Potatoes, Tomatoes, Blueberries, Firebrand Berries and Horseshoe Crabs.[/*]
[*][b]Wild animals:[/b] Wolf, Stag, Siren, Boar, Winged Brood and Bear, the animals whose skulls, claws, tusks and antlers upgrade your gear.[/*]
[*][b]Enemies:[/b] every faction the daily and weekly "Kill N" challenges can ask for: The Risen, Nith, Prisoners, Boarskin, Plagued, Knights of Tanth, False Ones, Balak Taw, Harvesters and Giants.[/*]
[*][b]Valuables (off by default):[/b] treasure chests, special (orange) shinies and Dire Nettles.[/*]
[*][b]Knows the world's state:[/b] areas change their enemies with your story progress and over time. A plain marker means "it is there"; a marker with a [b]?[/b] means "it can be there when you arrive". The [b]?[/b] button next to the panel's title hides all maybes. [url=https://github.com/vergir/NRftW-MapResourceMarkers/blob/main/docs/enemy-spawns.md]How enemy spawns work[/url] explains the rules (and how to find the enemy your challenge wants).[/*]
[*][b]Harvested, killed or looted:[/b] the marker gets a red cross until the game would bring it back, which happens when the fog creeps back over the spot.[/*]
[*][b]Caves:[/b] what is inside a cave or cellar shows at its entrance, with a doorway badge. Wait at a cave's entrance and its marker turns from [b]?[/b] to plain the moment the enemy you are after rolls in.[/*]
[*][b]Above or below:[/b] near you, markers get the game's own height arrows, like quest and bounty icons.[/*]
[*][b]Unlocks as you go:[/b] a button appears once the story allows that type in your world, and turns grey while none is around right now.[/*]
[*][b]Gamepad and keyboard:[/b] the D-pad and the left stick move through the panel like the game's own filters.[/*]
[*][b]Minimap:[/b] works with the Minimap mod, which shows the markers around you.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/LavaGang/MelonLoader/releases]MelonLoader[/url] 0.7.3 or newer.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install MelonLoader into the game folder and start the game once.[/*]
[*]Extract the mod's zip into the game folder, so that [i]MapResourceMarkers.dll[/i] ends up in the [i]Mods[/i] folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]Steam Deck / Linux (Proton):[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Copy the files from MelonLoader's [i]MelonLoader.x64.zip[/i] (the Windows build) into the game folder, and the mod into [i]Mods[/i].[/*]
[*]In Steam, open the game's Properties > General > Launch Options and enter:
[code]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="version=n,b" %command%[/code][/*]
[*]Start the game. On the first start MelonLoader installs the .NET runtime it needs by itself; that start takes a minute or two.[/*]
[/list]
[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [i]Mods\MapResourceMarkers.dll[/i]. Its settings stay in [i]UserData\MelonPreferences.cfg[/i]; delete the [MapResourceMarkers] section if you want them gone too. Nothing in the save was changed, so nothing needs cleaning up.

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]
In [i]Options > Gameplay[/i]:
[list]
[*][b]Resource Markers in Unexplored Areas[/b] (default on): also show markers in parts of the map you have not explored yet. This might spoil the fun of exploring.[/*]
[*][b]Resource Marker Size[/b] (50% to 200%).[/*]
[*][b]Map Markers: Harvesting / Cooking / Wild Animals / Enemies / Valuables[/b]: which groups of buttons the panel has. Cooking and Valuables are off by default; Valuables shows where loot is, which might feel like cheating.[/*]
[/list]
In [i]UserData\MelonPreferences.cfg[/i], section [MapResourceMarkers], also: [b]Enabled[/b] (master switch), [b]AddSettingsRows[/b] (the rows in Options), [b]Debug[/b] (logs details for bug reports).

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Game version:[/b] made for No Rest for the Wicked "The Breach", tested with build 29466 and MelonLoader 0.7.3 on Windows, with a gamepad and with keyboard and mouse.[/*]
[*][b]After a game update:[/b] the markers come from the game's own world data, so new or moved nodes and spawns show up by themselves. If a patch changes the map screen, the panel may stop working; the rest of the game is not affected and the MelonLoader log says what failed.[/*]
[*][b]Co-op and saves:[/b] display only: nothing in the game simulation or your save is changed.[/*]
[*][b]Other mods:[/b] works with Minimap; no known conflicts.[/*]
[*][b]Language:[/b] button names are the game's own words in your language (item names, enemy types); the panel title, the setting names and "none right now" are English.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Source and support[/b][/size]
Source code, changelog and issue tracker: [url=https://github.com/vergir/NRftW-MapResourceMarkers]GitHub[/url] · License: MIT
Problems: the [b]Bugs[/b] tab here or a GitHub issue; please include the [i]MelonLoader\Latest.log[/i] file (with [i]Debug = true[/i] if you can) and the game build (shown in the main menu's corner). A marker in the wrong place: a screenshot of the map with the hero near it is enough.


[color=#999999]=============================== NEXUS "SUMMARY" FIELD ===============================
Choose trees, ores, fish, herbs, animals, enemy factions or chests in the map's Filters, and the map shows where they are.
=====================================================================================[/color]
